Z||000006||LuckyTheyWereEverMade||12-21-2000||01:57 AM||||JohnnyK,<P>It still better to lose to a minivan than drive one.  <P>Everybody is so focused on racing, but how does winning a drag race differ from losing one?  Are our egos so needy that we have to beat everyone we see? Drag races that are not an even match are boring. <P>I say you had a blast in that race, and a clean victory would have been a lot less fun.  Next time, race a 1984 minivan and I know you will win.<P> ||||reg||7
Z||000007||FieroSTETZ||12-21-2000||03:05 AM||||there are some minivans to look out for though, my mom has an aerostar with the optional 4.xl v6 and fat back tires, and it chirps on shifts. chevy astros powered by the 4.3l v6 can have a 350 bolted right in no problem, and some older dodge caravans were powered by mitsubishi 2.5l turbo motors, theres one that was posated her a long time ago that ran 13's- now, one of those huge 80's van conversions, should be easy kills? mini vans would make excellent sleepers.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1012904&a=7460757&p=25516673&Sequence=0&res=high"> ||||reg||1
